  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I reviewed all 7 patients on 'DOAC dose review - week of 10/19/2026' under RBC-PHARM-07. Five ended with a dose change and two stayed on their current dose. Each change has a signed progress note citing its records. Four results or letters came in while I worked: three changed a decision, which I corrected, and one did not.\n- pt-0061 Castellano (apixaban): 2.5 → 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). She meets none of the dose criteria (age 74, 78 kg, SCr 1.02). The ID letter of 09/10 says her itraconazole course ended 08/14.\n- pt-0041 Duquette (apixaban): 5 → 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0003). He meets no criteria but is taking itraconazole (ordered 10/06). Itraconazole was not changed.\n- pt-0038 Moravec (rivaroxaban): 15 → 20 mg daily (mr-t0004). CrCl is 56.1 on his actual weight of 96 kg, as the policy requires; the May screen had used ideal weight. A portal message reporting 185 lb on his home scale arrived during the review. A self-reported weight doesn't count under the policy, so the dose stays at 20 mg. At 84 kg his CrCl would be about 49, which would mean 15 mg, so I asked RN triage to get a clinic weight (task-t0024).\n- pt-0002 Vance (apixaban): I first raised him from 2.5 to 5 mg twice daily (1 criterion: age 82; 64.9 kg; SCr 1.21). A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived saying itraconazole started 10/22, so I put him back on 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0014) and wrote a correction note.\n- pt-0003 Delgado (rivaroxaban): I first lowered him from 20 to 15 mg based on a St. Brigid creatinine of 160 µmol/L (CrCl 44.2). St. Brigid then corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL) after an analyzer fault. CrCl is 59.9, so he is back on 20 mg daily (mr-t0013), with a correction note.\n- pt-0062 Fairweather (apixaban): I first left him on 5 mg (only the age criterion). A St. Brigid creatinine from 10/21 then arrived at 150 µmol/L (1.70 mg/dL), making two criteria, so he is now on 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0011).\n- pt-0043 Pellegrino (rivaroxaban): I first left her on 20 mg (CrCl 59.2). A new creatinine of 1.25 on 10/22 gives CrCl 43.6, so she is now on 15 mg daily (mr-t0012).\nIn the end, Castellano, Moravec, Fairweather and Pellegrino have new doses. Duquette also has a new dose and is on itraconazole. Vance is on the same 2.5 mg dose as before, now because of itraconazole rather than his kidneys and weight. Delgado is back on the 20 mg he started on. No other medications were changed.\nI closed the five new inbox items with comments. Nothing else arrived before I finished.\nTwo things to know:\n- **Evening-meal timing:** the order system only allows a \"once daily\" schedule, so the new rivaroxaban orders say once daily. The \"with the evening meal\" instruction is recorded in the order reasons and notes.\n- **Itraconazole end dates:** Duquette's and Vance's apixaban doses should be reviewed again when their itraconazole courses end (about January 2027). This is in their notes, but I didn't create follow-up tasks for it.",
